# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores text as LF. Enforce it explicitly so line endings do
# not vary per clone (core.autocrlf), which is the source of the recurring
# "CRLF will be replaced by LF" churn, and so shell scripts and git hooks keep
# a valid LF shebang under sh regardless of the checkout platform.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises every text file to LF both in the repository
# and in the working tree. MATLAB/Octave and Python read LF correctly on all
# platforms, so a forced-LF working tree is safe here and keeps Windows and
# Linux (CI) byte-identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that MUST stay LF in the working tree to remain executable under sh.
*.sh          text eol=lf
.githooks/**  text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise or diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mat  binary
*.mex* binary
*.ico  binary
